  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Demand for Buda Juice’s ultra‑fresh cold‑pressed beverages remains strong, with all recent revenue growth coming from deeper penetration of its existing customer base—a sign of brand loyalty and repeat purchase. A major new Walmart distribution rollout marks a leap into mass retail, broadening the brand’s reach. Temporary lime cost inflation weighed on margins, but the underlying category momentum in the fresh perimeter is intact, with no mention of softening consumer demand or competitive disruption.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management capped its first full quarter as a public company by executing on a mid‑teen growth outlook, beating profit expectations, and delivering sharply higher free cash flow. The Walmart expansion signals disciplined national account execution, while the focus on organic growth from current customers suggests a conservative, loyalty‐driven approach. Commentary highlighted the scalability of the proprietary cold‑chain platform, and an investor letter referenced a long growth runway, indicating early credibility with niche institutional investors.",
